  "summary": "Design canonical skill 3.3.0 -> 3.4.0: mirrors the dev lifecycle's approval pattern split (bundle 09e72961-134c-4597-8e0c-45c1e93264dd). New patterns/approval-sign-off.md enumerates design's ~25 existing 'Stop and wait' checkpoints (Frame through Publish, plus the per-phase Announce/Compact/Resume triad) as a fixed, unconditional sign-off list -- design never had a centralized approvals file before, so this is additive, not a rename. New patterns/approval-intelligent.md defines the same narrower auto-approve mechanism as dev's: state the materiality criterion first, escalate on any doubt, or auto-approve with a mandatory logged rationale -- never touching a gate on approval-sign-off.md's fixed list. One designated checkpoint wired so far: Frame Step 3's tracker assign/transition, the exact structural analog of dev's Ceremony Step 1 (same tracker mechanism, same auto-approve criterion: unassigned or already-the-user's and in a pre-work status auto-approves; otherwise escalates).",
